<article class="env-lemma" id="0GP1">
  <p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/0GP1">Lemma <span data-tag="0GP1">56.3.9</span>.</a> Let $R$ be a ring. Let $A$ and $B$ be $R$-algebras. If </p>
  <div class="equation">
  \[  F : \text{Mod}_ A \longrightarrow \text{Mod}_ B  \]
</div>
  <p> is an $R$-linear equivalence of categories, then there exists an isomorphism $A \to B$ of $R$-algebras and an invertible $B$-module $L$ such that $F$ is isomorphic to the functor $M \mapsto (M \otimes _ A B) \otimes _ B L$. </p>
</article><article class="env-proof">
    <p>
      <strong>Proof.</strong>
      We get $A \to B$ and $L$ from Lemma <a href="/tag/0GP0" data-tag="0GP0">56.3.8</a>. To finish the proof, we need to show that the $R$-linearity of $F$ forces $A \to B$ to be an $R$-algebra map. We omit the details. 
      <span class="qed">$\square$</span>
    </p>
</article>